CVSA is Civitas Resources, an oil and gas company in Colorado, so it does not belong in a for-profit education theme. The ticker may be a mix-up with Covista or another education name, but the "Healthcare education & nursing programs" description doesn't match any CVSA business I know of. The other three, LAUR (Laureate Education), STRA (Strategic Education) and LOPE (Grand Canyon Education), are all postsecondary education companies.

The thesis is cut off at "CVSA's rec…", which suggests CVSA is tied to the theme's news. The description supplied for CVSA is education-related, and the thesis groups it with the other education stocks. Since I'm uncertain about the ticker, the safer call is to go by the description given and keep it.

